  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rapid Article 6 Readiness and Needs Assessments for CTF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Active</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CTF Startup PIN #1 Context - Initial analysis is required for country teams and PIN approvers to understand national context and needs. GGGI is currently active or has completed support for Article 6 projects in 15 countries; in early consultations with additional countries - As a pilot, CPU has drafted a methodology based on MATS/DAPA/SPAR6C Programs, MAAP-ITR tool (World Bank), Article 6 Toolkit (NDC Partnership), but GGGI&apos;s Rapid Readiness Needs Assessment will be more simple and practical for country teams and government decision makers. Proposed Activities - Finalize methodology and publish it with a self-assessment tool as global public goods (building on existing draft methodology) - Implement methodology by doing 15 Rapid Readiness and Needs Assessments Results - Improve stakeholder understanding of their national situations and needs - Improve evidence base for Readiness Facility to make decisions on funding Readiness PINs - Global public goods as a quick win for CTF - Accelerated PIN development to meet goal of at least 5 in-country PINs by September</narrative>
  </description>
